"opening": "The more-itertools library currently exhibits several regressions and incorrect behaviors in its public API functions. These issues affect input validation, iteration logic, and edge case handling for users relying on these utilities.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m01",
"text": "The interleave_evenly function must correctly handle empty iterables without raising errors or producing unexpected results. When provided with empty inputs, it should yield no items gracefully."
},
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "The sliced function must raise a ValueError when a negative slice size is provided. This ensures that invalid arguments are caught early rather than causing undefined behavior."
},
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "The numeric_range.__reversed__ method must not raise an error when called on an empty range. It should return an empty iterator consistent with standard Python range behavior."
},
{
"id": "m04",
"text": "The numeric_range.__reversed__ method must preserve the correct sequence of values during reverse iteration. The reversed output must accurately reflect the original range's values in descending order."
}
]
}
